# Ship docs and site with every new feature

> **ABSOLUTE**: User-facing functionality is not done until it is documented on [getax.wenneker.io](https://getax.wenneker.io) and in the repo README. Agents must update docs in the **same change** as the feature — not as a follow-up.

## When this applies

Any change that adds or materially changes:

- CLI subcommands or flags (`crates/ax-cli/`)
- MCP tools (`crates/ax-mcp/`)
- Command Center / `ax web` pages (`crates/ax-web/web-ui/`)
- Policy rules, skills, or workflows (`.ax/policy/`, `crates/ax-policy/`)

## Required checklist (end of every feature task)

```text
1. site/src/content/docs/     — guide and/or reference page updated
2. site/src/content/docs/reference/cli.md — every new/changed command has a bash example
3. site/src/content/docs/reference/mcp-server.md — new MCP tools listed
4. README.md                  — command table + one-line description if CLI/MCP changed
5. site/src/pages/index.astro — homepage features/slogan if the feature is headline-worthy
6. site/astro.config.mjs      — sidebar link when adding a new guide
```

## CLI reference rule

Every command section in `reference/cli.md` must include at least one copy-pasteable example block:

```bash
ax <command> ...
```

Hidden/internal commands (`serve`, `prompt-hook`, …) are exempt.

## Release alignment

When cutting a release, bump version strings in:

- `site/public/releases/latest.txt`
- `site/src/content/docs/getting-started/introduction.md` (What's new)
- CLI page frontmatter description version

Do not pin unreleased versions in install scripts until the GitHub tag exists.

## Forbidden

- Marking feature work complete with only code merged
- Adding CLI/MCP surface without README + site reference
- Leaving `next-steps` or introduction links broken (`/ax/` prefix is wrong — use Starlight slugs)
